Found while reviewing k185. Skilletor::Resolver builds codex_home from $ENV{CODEX_HOME} and claude_config_dir from $ENV{CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR} as raw bytes (perl/lib/Skilletor/Resolver.pm:40, :56), while HOME (CLI.pm:135) and HERMES_HOME (Engine.pm hermes_home) go through decode_utf8_lossy. A non-ASCII CODEX_HOME or CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR may then be encoded twice on the way to the file system, or compare unequal to a decoded path. Not reproduced.

Done: both builders decode as HOME and HERMES_HOME do, with a test that syncs under a non-ASCII CODEX_HOME and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (and, if the reference agrees, a conformance case).
